# `project - rename` with spaces (D-026): DS0104 with a fix; it still parses as project-rename.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | project - rename total = amount
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..52
  PIPELINE@0..51
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    PROJECT_RENAME_OP@20..51
      IDENT@20..27 "project"
      WHITESPACE@27..28 " "
      MINUS@28..29 "-"
      WHITESPACE@29..30 " "
      IDENT@30..36 "rename"
      WHITESPACE@36..37 " "
      RENAME_ITEM@37..51
        NAME@37..42
          IDENT@37..42 "total"
        WHITESPACE@42..43 " "
        EQ@43..44 "="
        WHITESPACE@44..45 " "
        NAME_REF@45..51
          IDENT@45..51 "amount"
  WHITESPACE@51..52 "\n"

error[DS0104]: operator name `project - rename` has spaces in it
  --> query:1:21
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | project - rename total = amount
  |                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ an operator name is one word
  |
  = help: write `project-rename`, with no spaces

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | project-rename total = amount
which parses without errors
